{"event_type":"review","id":"6fa37cfda4b4962b4ee8892d2e0db2fe25a1610707098c6696c898d0a7a9628e","occurred_at":"2026-11-12T00:46:13Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/799580cf5d25586a163930ff1957e7022299668b93988830e7f48c2b58959d9c","sha256":"799580cf5d25586a163930ff1957e7022299668b93988830e7f48c2b58959d9c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/93bafc7715f0395c426db9531d35b2614c8c33615851d8e02969223e1c7d8110","sha256":"93bafc7715f0395c426db9531d35b2614c8c33615851d8e02969223e1c7d8110"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0e0bdb6a9dbce1e81f0578bb74720dfef4e1e7288af2cfb58f9e414e2b319413","sha256":"0e0bdb6a9dbce1e81f0578bb74720dfef4e1e7288af2cfb58f9e414e2b319413"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/dcb09c3e922dfa074aa003e36c514f8456ba7ce8a1761cf1aac380029acb9afc","sha256":"dcb09c3e922dfa074aa003e36c514f8456ba7ce8a1761cf1aac380029acb9afc"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/231e8bed472259984f2440f17ee260681d151fe21f6bbc414186a38a88a5b575","sha256":"231e8bed472259984f2440f17ee260681d151fe21f6bbc414186a38a88a5b575"}],"attempt_id":"9f68bcb084d9499c702ea2530d29b09ab1cf893ccfd0f3628330ac5dc744fa31:0:1","base":"1451579c06e4b982baa1a160393f6b9900165b5a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"8c9ce3535b26b371c640a25884615395d80d9d5a","body":"**Follow-up: return JSON for argument errors.**\n\nA missing subcommand or required option exits here before `_print()`. Default `argparse` writes usage to stderr and exits with status 2, so this path produces no JSON artifact. ([docs.python.org](https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/argparse.html?utm_source=openai)) The parser also rejects `--json`.\n\nAdd machine-mode parsing and return the required JSON usage-error object.\n\nAs per coding guidelines, I1 requires “Every operation invocation writes machine-readable JSON to stdout.” Based on learnings, the owner's policy defers “P2/Minor findings” to follow-up issues.","id":"6f56aa52bd83c1b822f345f2fa94b6662240165815ba82f45b5c9c31be7bd97f","intervals":[[180,180]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/unit-switch.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Follow-up: return JSON for argument errors."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"749333d6ce5ac667fac8927245b723a583484b09","body":"**Guard `partial_reset_repair()` before it unlinks files.**\n\n`partial-inspect` dispatches directly to `partial_inspect()`, which calls `partial_reset_repair()` as its first statement. That function unlinks each existing repair unit, staged, trigger, and marker path. The `phase_prepare()` nodename check in the base module is never reached on this path, and the base module import does not run it.\n\nRunning `partial-inspect` outside the `crq-probe` guest can remove installed repair units and their state files. Add the same check that `phase_prepare()` uses before the first unlink. The check covers every caller of `partial_reset_repair()`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def partial_reset_repair():\n     \"\"\"Reset the repair topology without touching any retained record or log.\"\"\"\n+    require(os.uname().nodename == \"crq-probe\",\n+            \"partial proof driver only runs on the disposable crq-probe guest\")\n     UNIT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n```\n\n</details>","id":"71e02156c66d9eccb4a4f67f84f87d2d2c7f149fe8fe54b18bd2e7958efc2776","intervals":[[197,197]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch-guest-partial.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Guard `partialresetrepair()` before it unlinks files."}],"head":"3b1000ccebd027944fbe95adf44cccec09da96d7","head_tree":"fd9b086373c60203765fe780f899178a146a7825","input_scope":[{"blob":"72a5adc7e73ed53367e862f1ee1